1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
No!

5
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
So strong!

6
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,000
What kind of magic is this?

7
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Now, how should you die?

8
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Please! Please spare us! We'll never attack another village again! I swear!

9
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Maybe I won't kill you this time.

10
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Huh?

11
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Since it is a special day.

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,000
The day that an angel was born.

13
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Go on. I want to hear you wish her a happy birthday.

14
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Who is that?

15
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Celebrate her with every fiber of your being, before you die.

16
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
So you are gonna kill us!

17
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
they were gonna kill us, bro?

18
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:59,980
Thank you.

19
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:29,980
Thank you.

20
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:59,980
Thank you.

21
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Thank you.

22
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Thank you.

23
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,720
Knowing him, he's being reckless and getting into all kinds of trouble.

24
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:36,980
But it's all right!

25
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:38,820
You can come home any time, Asta!

26
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:40,400
Let's see.

27
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:45,060
He says, dear sister, fellow church orphans, and Hajj village chief.

28
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:46,580
What am I, shop liver?

29
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:51,480
Asta's made it to junior magic knight third class!

30
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:52,060
What?

31
00:03:54,460 --> 00:03:55,700
Good job, Asta.

32
00:03:56,180 --> 00:03:57,520
Glad you're not slacking off.

33
00:03:58,340 --> 00:04:00,100
I knew you could do it, Asta!

34
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:04,040
You boys take care of yourselves and keep doing us proud, you hear?

35
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:14,400
You know, I've heard that you've been promoted to magic knight first class.

36
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:15,240
Congratulations!

37
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:17,820
It's not really a big deal.

38
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:19,040
Exactly right.

39
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:21,360
We can't have you getting a big head.

40
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:24,880
Never forget that I am your better in both rank and experience.

41
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:31,200
Is everything all right, sir?

42
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:34,680
Take it.

43
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:39,500
A promotion gift from your superior.

44
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,160
You keep that for yourself.

45
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:44,060
I know where all your earnings go.

46
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:48,800
He doesn't always know how to express his emotions.

47
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:51,240
I wish you'd gotten to see it, though.

48
00:04:51,580 --> 00:04:53,740
He was so happy when he heard about your promotion.

49
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:55,640
I think his glasses were sparkling.

50
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:57,700
That's pathetic.

51
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:08,000
All right, I need everyone to listen up.

52
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:12,200
Our wages have come in, so there's no work today.

53
00:05:12,540 --> 00:05:13,060
Yeah!

54
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:17,260
Okay, time to get training!

55
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:20,500
Yummy, sir!

56
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:21,720
Thank you!

57
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,400
Great call as usual!

58
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:24,580
Time for a drink!

59
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:25,560
Or three!

60
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:28,240
Well, you know what that calls for?

61
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:28,880
Check it!

62
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:32,920
All right, it's time to get busy!

63
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:34,460
Ladies, hey there!

64
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:35,860
Who's your guy?

65
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:37,220
Me!

66
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:41,020
Oh, yeah, Ghosh.

67
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:42,580
That bandit thing yesterday?

68
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:43,480
Good job.

69
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:46,180
Today is my little sister Marie's birthday.

70
00:05:46,340 --> 00:05:49,060
Do you think I could extend my time off until her next birthday?

71
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:49,980
Hell no.

72
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:50,580
Free time?

73
00:05:50,860 --> 00:05:53,220
Man, I hope somebody attacks the capital again!

74
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:54,100
Oh, hey!

75
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:55,700
Maybe I should do it!

76
00:05:55,820 --> 00:05:57,140
That's an even bigger no.

77
00:05:59,140 --> 00:06:01,600
I guess nobody feels like working.

78
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:02,160
Hey!

79
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:02,660
Hey!

80
00:06:04,220 --> 00:06:06,120
Kat's creation magic!

81
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:07,820
Feed me, sheep cook!

82
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:23,240
Stuffed my face!

83
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:23,920
Yeah!

84
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:26,120
Hot potatoes!

85
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:27,260
No way!

86
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:30,040
They're a specialty of ours village!

87
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:33,160
That's where my darling friendship for visitors is from!

88
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:34,520
Give it my try!

89
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:35,880
So good!

90
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:37,400
Thank you!

91
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:39,600
They're pretty dense.

92
00:06:39,740 --> 00:06:41,140
Must be really high in fiber.

93
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:45,020
Oh, it's super crumbly!

94
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:48,500
Amazing how it sucks out of moisture out of your mouth.

95
00:06:49,060 --> 00:06:51,180
These would make for a pretty good bar snack.

96
00:06:53,540 --> 00:06:54,020
Sure!

97
00:06:54,020 --> 00:07:06,420
What present would be a worthy tribute to my little goddess on her birthday?

98
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:07,980
It's time.

99
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:10,280
Ladies of the Clover Kingdom, get ready.

100
00:07:10,420 --> 00:07:10,860
Here comes...

101
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:11,000
Wait!

102
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,180
Oh, right, of course.

103
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:16,580
You'll be wanting me to take you into town for another match, huh, Captain?

104
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:17,380
Yep.

105
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:18,840
But first...

106
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:21,580
All that fiber must have kicked in.

107
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:24,380
I might push past my limits right here.

108
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:27,380
That's one limit you do not need to push past, sir!

109
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:28,800
So gross!

110
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:33,460
What now?

111
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:36,820
I get a day off out of nowhere and there's nothing to do.

112
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:38,400
Magnus, sir!

113
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:38,960
Hmm?

114
00:07:39,180 --> 00:07:40,400
Sorry to bother you, sir!

115
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:43,720
But if you have time, will you please take me somewhere on your awesome broom?

116
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:44,360
Oh?

117
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:48,300
How can I say no when you ask how sweet and polite like that, Rasta?

118
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:49,560
Where to?

119
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:50,700
Neon, sir!

120
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:51,640
Wait!

121
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:52,940
I know that place!

122
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:56,040
It's where the boys went for that stupid mixer!

123
00:07:58,800 --> 00:07:59,800
Sure.

124
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:01,360
So, what you going there for?

125
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:02,600
Well, uh...

126
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:03,700
Well, what?

127
00:08:04,140 --> 00:08:05,780
I think we could talk on the way.

128
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:07,240
Oh, come on!

129
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:08,900
Not that I care what he does!

130
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:11,520
Or who he may or may not be going to see!

131
00:08:11,820 --> 00:08:13,880
It's simple curiosity, that's all!

132
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:15,900
Well, are you coming?

133
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:16,420
What?

134
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:17,200
Like, now?

135
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:18,980
Now or never, it's your call, dude.

136
00:08:19,060 --> 00:08:19,640
Now is good!

137
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,940
Get ready and hold on tight!

138
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:23,940
Huh?

139
00:08:24,940 --> 00:08:26,100
Oh, yeah!

140
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:32,040
Okay, so maybe I do care!

141
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:45,200
Greetings, my darling sister Marie.

142
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:48,600
I've just arrived in the village where you live.

143
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:49,800
Let's get out of here.

144
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:51,640
Being a magic knight isn't easy.

145
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:54,400
But I don't mind because I'm doing it for you.

146
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:57,820
And with my wages, I can buy you the presents you deserve.

147
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:11,380
Me, a former prisoner, living a life on the straight and narrow?

148
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:15,420
It's thanks to you, Marie, my angel-made flesh.

149
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:16,960
I do it for you.

150
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:23,080
My nose won't stop bleeding.

151
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:24,560
Gosh, sir!

152
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:26,760
We've been waiting for you.

153
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:30,700
If you would please step inside, we have presents ready for your perusal.

154
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:32,680
Show me immediately.

155
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:34,660
Right away!

156
00:09:35,180 --> 00:09:36,320
First up, these!

157
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:37,740
Perfect for a little girl.

158
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:39,660
They all just love stuffed animals.

159
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:43,040
One of these would be sure to put a smile on her face.

160
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:46,860
They're perfect.

161
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:48,440
Thanks so much.

162
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:53,080
Yes, I'll take them all.

163
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:53,940
Certainly, sir.

164
00:09:54,380 --> 00:09:55,340
Our next item.

165
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:59,440
She'll be playing with us for hours, imagining herself living in such a place.

166
00:09:59,780 --> 00:10:02,420
A perfect home she'd share with her brother, naturally.

167
00:10:05,420 --> 00:10:06,480
Big brother!

168
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:10,000
I'm so glad you're home!

169
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:14,600
I'll take that, too.

170
00:10:15,040 --> 00:10:15,800
Excellent, sir!

171
00:10:16,180 --> 00:10:20,360
Last but not least, with this costume, your sister can be a real angel.

172
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:25,120
You know, Gosh.

173
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:26,820
I love you.

174
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,480
The whole store, I want it all.

175
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:35,980
Always a pleasure, sir.

176
00:10:35,980 --> 00:10:40,060
What?

177
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:42,600
You're visiting some girl you met at a mixer?

178
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:43,860
Sure am.

179
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:47,400
I promised Rebecca I'd come play with her brothers and sisters sometime.

180
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:48,360
Go, Asta.

181
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:52,100
You're a fast mover, already bringing the whole family in on your date.

182
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:53,640
I'm proud of you, buddy.

183
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:54,660
Yeah!

184
00:10:54,980 --> 00:10:56,660
Hey, look, Neon's up ahead.

185
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,200
All right!

186
00:10:58,360 --> 00:11:00,840
I'm going to play so hard, they won't know what hit them!

187
00:11:00,900 --> 00:11:02,520
Oh, take it easy, boy.

188
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:03,020
All right!

189
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:16,800
Greetings, my beloved little sister Marie.

190
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:20,980
Please forgive your brother whose blood loss has made him tardy.

191
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:23,360
I've brought you so many birthday presents.

192
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:25,980
I hope they will bring you great joy.

193
00:11:25,980 --> 00:11:32,520
All my wages are gone now, but no price is too high for your happiness.

194
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:37,140
Soon I'll see my precious angel again.

195
00:11:38,140 --> 00:11:40,340
And that smiling face of hers.

196
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:42,600
Ah, my darling Marie.

197
00:11:43,260 --> 00:11:43,720
Marie.

198
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:44,720
Marie.

199
00:11:45,300 --> 00:11:45,540
Marie.

200
00:11:45,540 --> 00:11:52,660
You like that, huh, Marie?

201
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:54,960
So fun!

202
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:56,880
You're really strong, Asta!

203
00:11:58,340 --> 00:11:59,740
I want to turn!

204
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:00,660
Me too!

205
00:12:00,740 --> 00:12:01,920
Okay, come on and...

206
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:02,220
Ah!

207
00:12:02,220 --> 00:12:09,020
Get away from her right now, you scum!

208
00:12:10,140 --> 00:12:12,420
Oh, it's the Bloody Nose Sister Lover!

209
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:15,500
Call me a Bloody Nose Sister Lover again, Meathead.

210
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:16,480
I'll squash you!

211
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,460
That isn't going to happen!

212
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:19,960
Not the way I've been training!

213
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:21,880
Shut up!

214
00:12:22,420 --> 00:12:26,980
I only get to see my sister once a month, which means these visits are sacrosanct.

215
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:32,020
Today I set aside all of their thoughts, ready to dote on my Marie in every way possible.

216
00:12:32,500 --> 00:12:34,740
It was supposed to be flirty and fun and perfect!

217
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:37,500
So how is it that you showed up here before me?

218
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:40,660
So you do have a sister complex and get nosebleeds.

219
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:43,100
And how was I supposed to know she was your sister?

220
00:12:43,740 --> 00:12:46,300
Stop pointing your grubby little finger at my angel!

221
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:48,880
I know I showed you her picture, don't lie!

222
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:49,580
Did you?

223
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:50,460
I don't remember.

224
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:54,420
I met her today when I came over to Rebecca's to play with her brothers and sisters.

225
00:12:54,660 --> 00:12:55,360
Uh, hi.

226
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:57,240
He's really scary.

227
00:12:57,840 --> 00:12:59,120
What's flirty, Meathead?

228
00:12:59,140 --> 00:13:00,360
I don't know that word.

229
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:00,820
Shh!

230
00:13:01,020 --> 00:13:03,560
Well, Marie's cute, that's for sure.

231
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:07,800
Of course she's cute, but that doesn't mean you have permission to make eyes at my sister,

232
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:08,500
you filth!

233
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:10,800
Stop it, brother!

234
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:13,640
I don't want you doing mean things to him!

235
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:16,600
Please, Osta's going to be my husband someday!

236
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:18,900
Osta's going to be my husband someday!

237
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:20,860
Osta's going to be my husband someday!

238
00:13:21,060 --> 00:13:23,020
Osta's going to be my husband someday!

239
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:29,460
Her husband!

240
00:13:30,140 --> 00:13:33,600
When I tagged along with them, that was not what I was expecting!

241
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:36,640
Uh, the fair, miss?

242
00:13:37,340 --> 00:13:38,440
Will this be enough?

243
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:40,420
Heck yeah!

244
00:13:40,900 --> 00:13:41,260
Kill.

245
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:42,360
Kill.

246
00:13:42,660 --> 00:13:43,300
Kill.

247
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:43,680
You okay?

248
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:44,620
Kill.

249
00:13:45,100 --> 00:13:45,580
Kill.

250
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:47,380
Kill now!

251
00:13:47,380 --> 00:13:51,980
Mirror magic!

252
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:54,420
Reflect ray!

253
00:13:57,960 --> 00:13:59,980
Hey, what are you doing with that mirror?

254
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:01,160
Now die.

255
00:14:02,160 --> 00:14:02,700
Whoa!

256
00:14:04,660 --> 00:14:05,720
Please stop!

257
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:06,660
Don't hurt him!

258
00:14:07,160 --> 00:14:07,880
Oh my.

259
00:14:08,300 --> 00:14:10,400
It's awfully noisy out here.

260
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:13,300
Marie, it's time to go.

261
00:14:13,620 --> 00:14:15,260
You need to get back to the church now.

262
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:16,160
Sister.

263
00:14:16,940 --> 00:14:17,820
I see.

264
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:19,180
So you're here, Ghosh.

265
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:20,560
That's right, Hag.

266
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,420
That's sister to you.

267
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:24,000
Mind your manners.

268
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:26,500
Marie and I are going on a date.

269
00:14:26,860 --> 00:14:28,760
You can head back to the church on your own.

270
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:29,640
No, Ghosh.

271
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:30,660
She's coming.

272
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:33,340
The sooner you accept that, the better for us all.

273
00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:37,960
When are you going to realize that you're no good for an impressionable young girl like

274
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:38,340
Marie?

275
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:43,800
She deserves to be around somebody better than you, with your bad attitude and nasty tongue.

276
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:45,680
What was that, you old croon?

277
00:14:45,780 --> 00:14:46,580
There, see?

278
00:14:46,700 --> 00:14:47,480
